# 6. Operations Tool (v5) — Capability Summary

OTB_Ops_Tool_v5.html is the current operational tool. Single self-contained HTML file with browser-local persistence. Auto-migrates v4 data on first open.

### Core Capabilities

- Site plan / plat / Google Maps image upload as background layer. Auto-compressed to max 2400px JPEG 85%.

- Image editor: rotate (90° L / 90° R / 180°), crop (draw rectangle, apply, repeat), reset, apply & save.

- Draw mode for units and parking stalls. Drag-to-move, drag-to-resize with 8-corner handles.

- Snap-to-neighbor toggle. When On, dragging snaps to butt-against and edge-aligned positions within 8 SVG units.

- Three parking lots pre-configured with fill order. Editable.

- Per-stall: lot assignment, status (open / reserved / out-of-service), reservedFor (link to tenant).

- Pylon sign: photo + tenant slot list with top-to-bottom order + per-slot approval status.

- Per-unit exterior signage: photo + approval workflow (pending / approved / rejected / installed).

- POI layer: 38 categories / 8 groups (Utilities / HVAC / Plumbing / Life Safety / Site / Building / Other) — water meters, water shutoffs, gas / electric, HVAC RTUs, grease traps, fire hydrants, FDC, knox boxes, AEDs, dumpsters, benches, etc.

- Per-POI: status (operational / needs-service / out-of-service), last serviced, next due, vendor, photo, notes.

- Per-unit floor plan upload (multi-floor supported) with pan/zoom viewer.

- Heat map modes: Status, Lease Expiration, Rent $/SF, Size (SF).

- Filter chips, search, sort, auto-fit, JSON export/import, reset to SOT.

