# 11. Insurance & Risk Management

## 11.1 Required Coverage

| **Coverage** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- |
| **Commercial Property** | Special form; replacement cost; verify TIV current |
| **Wind / Named Peril** | Verify deductible (often separate, %-of-value); critical in LA |
| **Flood (NFIP and/or private)** | Required per lender; verify flood zone; consider excess flood |
| **Commercial General Liability** | $1M / $2M minimum; higher recommended |
| **Umbrella / Excess Liability** | $5M+ recommended for retail center |
| **Ordinance or Law** | Coverage A (loss to undamaged portion), B (demolition), C (increased cost of construction) |
| **Business Income / Rent Loss** | 12+ months minimum |
| **Equipment Breakdown** | HVAC, electrical, mechanical |
| **Pollution Legal Liability** | If environmental risk identified |
| **Cyber Liability** | If collecting tenant data / online payments |
| **Crime / Fidelity** | Employee dishonesty coverage |
| **EPLI** | If employees — employment practices |

## 11.2 Tenant Insurance Requirements

- Each tenant maintains CGL $1M / $2M minimum

- Belle Realty of Lafayette, LLC named as additional insured on tenant CGL

- Workers' compensation per LA law where employees present

- Property insurance on tenant's improvements and personal property

- Annual COI collection and audit

- **Special requirements — food tenants: **Jason's, Graze, Great American Cookies — product liability

- **Special requirements — HotWorx: **health-club style exposures

- **Special requirements — Cat Clinic: **professional liability / animal handling

- **Special requirements — Upstream Rehab: **healthcare professional liability

## 11.3 COI Tracking

- DoorLoop COI tracker active for all tenants

- Quarterly audit of expiring COIs

- Default-notice protocol for non-current COIs

- Vendor COI audit — same cadence

# 12. Emergency & Hurricane Response Plan

*Hurricane season: June 1 – November 30. Lafayette has experienced direct strikes and major windstorm events. Pre-season preparation is mandatory; in-season response must be drilled.*

## 12.1 Emergency Contacts — First Call Tree

| **Contact** | **Number** |
| --- | --- |
| **Property Manager (24/7) — Adam Abdalla** | 337-288-5411 |
| **Lafayette Police (non-emergency)** | 337-291-8600 |
| **Lafayette Parish Sheriff** | 337-232-9211 |
| **Lafayette Fire (non-emergency)** | 337-291-8716 |
| **Acadian Ambulance / EMS** | 911 |
| **LUS Emergency (Electric/Water)** | 337-291-9200 |
| **Atmos Gas Leak** | 866-322-8667 |
| **Lafayette Consolidated Government** | 337-291-8000 |
| **Insurance Broker** | _____________________ |
| **Property Counsel** | _____________________ |
| **Water Mitigation Vendor** | _____________________ |
| **Roofing Emergency Tarp** | _____________________ |
| **Glass Storefront Emergency** | _____________________ |

## 12.2 Pre-Season Checklist (Complete by May 31)

- Insurance review with broker: wind/named-peril deductible, flood policy current, ordinance or law coverage adequate

- Confirm policy limits sufficient for total insurable value

- Photographic documentation: all building exteriors, signage, parking, mechanical equipment, common areas

- Update insurance schedule of values

- Roof inspection completed; minor repairs closed out

- Drainage / stormwater inlets clear; detention basin assessed

- Landscape trim: dead limbs removed; trees pruned near buildings/signs

- Pylon / monument sign structural inspection

- Loose items inventory (dumpsters, planters, A-frames) — securement plan

- Tenant communication: pre-season letter with hurricane plan, contacts, expectations

- Vendor confirmations: water mitigation, roofing, glass, electrical pre-positioned

- Master key inventory accessible off-site

- Cloud backup of property documents verified

## 12.3 Storm Approaching

### T-72 hours

- Monitor National Hurricane Center advisories

- Tenant notification — first advisory email

- Pre-position emergency vendor calls

- Bank: pre-fund operating account for processing delays

### T-48 hours

- Photograph property condition (timestamped) — baseline for claims

- Secure loose items — dumpsters chained, A-frames stored

- Tenant directive: shutdown procedures, board windows if Cat 3+, secure signage

- Confirm insurance broker reachable

### T-24 hours

- Final walk-through and photograph

- Confirm all tenants evacuating per their plans

- Office: data backup verified, critical docs in waterproof storage

- Disable non-essential exterior power if directed by LUS

## 12.4 Post-Storm Response

- Safety first: do not enter until LFD/LCG clears area

- Photograph all damage before any cleanup — every angle, every unit

- Video walk-through narrated with timestamps

- Notify insurance broker within 24 hours of accessing property

- Open claim file with policy number and damage inventory

- Emergency mitigation: water extraction, board-up, tarp — photograph before/during/after

- Save all receipts and invoices for emergency response (recoverable)

- Tenant communication: status, projected restoration timeline, rent abatement decisions

- Coordinate adjuster site visit

- Document Code Enforcement / FEMA / SBA interactions

- If federally declared disaster: explore SBA disaster loan for rebuild capital

## 12.5 Other Emergencies

### Water Leak (Interior)

- Isolate source — shut off water at main if needed

- Notify affected tenants

- Dispatch plumber / water mitigation

- Document with photos for insurance

### Fire

- 911

- Account for tenants / patrons — do not re-enter

- Notify insurance immediately upon LFD clearance

- Coordinate state fire marshal investigation

### Power Outage

- Confirm with LUS — area outage vs property-specific

- Tenant notification

- Emergency lighting check

- If extended: refrigeration tenants (**Jason****'****s Deli, Graze Acadiana, Great American Cookies**) priority.

### Security Incident

- 911 if active threat

- Preserve scene for LPD

- Pull CCTV footage immediately and preserve

- Tenant communication post-clearance

- Insurance notification if property damage

